  "summary": "Amazon CloudFront caches content at a global edge network in front of S3, load balancers, EC2 or VPC origins, with OAC, managed prefix lists, TTLs, invalidations and geo restriction. AWS Global Accelerator gives applications two static anycast IPs and carries TCP or UDP over the AWS backbone to healthy endpoints in several Regions. Includes CloudFront versus S3 Cross-Region Replication and CloudFront versus Global Accelerator.",
